WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.030 --> 00:00:05.190
It's exciting times for Disney fans as it's
finally been confirmed who'll be playing all

00:00:05.190 --> 00:00:09.610
the main parts in the star-studded remake
of Disney's animated classic The Lion King

00:00:09.610 --> 00:00:11.430
when it hits the big screen in 2019!

00:00:11.430 --> 00:00:15.929
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, it's Jan here,
and in this video, I'm going to run through

00:00:15.929 --> 00:00:19.680
all the details of the voice cast who'll be
playing the much-loved Lion King characters

00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:24.040
in director Jon Favreau's new take on the
1994 hit movie.

00:00:24.040 --> 00:00:29.200
Between his critically-acclaimed TV show Atlanta,
playing a young Lando Calrissian in the Han

00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:34.160
Solo movie, and starring as Simba in The Lion
King, the Emmy-award-winning Donald Glover

00:00:34.160 --> 00:00:35.780
is on fire right now.

00:00:35.780 --> 00:00:40.730
And frankly, I just can't wait for him to
be king in Disney's iconic musical!

00:00:40.730 --> 00:00:45.339
Speaking of music, in the animated movie,
Matthew Broderick only provided Simba's speaking

00:00:45.339 --> 00:00:47.609
voice, but didn't perform his songs.

00:00:47.609 --> 00:00:51.800
I'm sure Glover will make a tremendous new
Simba and he certainly won't have any trouble

00:00:51.800 --> 00:00:54.229
in the singing department either.

00:00:54.229 --> 00:00:58.620
On the subject of singing, none other than
Beyoncé is going to be lending her voice

00:00:58.620 --> 00:01:00.079
to the adult Nala.

00:01:00.079 --> 00:01:04.670
Yes, after turning down the role of the feather-duster
Plumette in the live-action Beauty And The

00:01:04.670 --> 00:01:09.290
Beast film, the modern Queen of Pop is taking
on a more suitable role as the Queen of the

00:01:09.290 --> 00:01:10.380
Pride Lands.

00:01:10.380 --> 00:01:16.010
Now, in the animated movie, adult Nala and
her mate Simba don't actually have that much

00:01:16.010 --> 00:01:20.610
to do when it comes to belting out songs,
but since the remake has cast two talented

00:01:20.610 --> 00:01:24.799
singers in those roles, I think we'll see
the range of songs expanded from the classics

00:01:24.799 --> 00:01:28.200
written by Elton John and Tim Rice for the
original movie.

00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:32.700
After all, that's what they did in Bill Condon's
recent version of Beauty And The Beast.

00:01:32.700 --> 00:01:36.799
And given Beyoncé and Glover's musical leanings,
I wouldn't be surprised if they'll have something

00:01:36.799 --> 00:01:38.510
of a hand in that themselves.

00:01:38.510 --> 00:01:44.090
It's fantastic to see James Earl Jones, aka
the voice of Darth Vader, returning to the

00:01:44.090 --> 00:01:48.909
role of Simba's father Mufasa, after he first
lent his vocal talents to the character in

00:01:48.909 --> 00:01:50.359
the animated movie.

00:01:50.359 --> 00:01:54.580
With Jones's incredible voice and powerful
style, I can't think of anyone better to play

00:01:54.580 --> 00:01:55.580
the role.

00:01:55.580 --> 00:01:57.100
The man is a legend!

00:01:57.100 --> 00:02:02.850
Given that the brilliant British actor Chiwetel
Ejiofor has been cast as Scar, I'm assuming

00:02:02.850 --> 00:02:06.770
that this version of Simba's uncle will be
continuing the long Hollywood tradition of

00:02:06.770 --> 00:02:11.340
villainous characters with English accents,
just as Jeremy Irons did back when he voiced

00:02:11.340 --> 00:02:13.720
the role in the original animation.

00:02:13.720 --> 00:02:17.709
If you're wondering where you've seen Ejiofor
previously, he gave an Oscar-nominated performance

00:02:17.709 --> 00:02:21.880
in 12 Years A Slave, and most recently, he
also starred in Marvel's Doctor Strange.

00:02:21.880 --> 00:02:25.620
Now, I just can't wait to hear his take on
Scar!

00:02:25.620 --> 00:02:29.700
Speaking of British actors, I presume that
talk-show host John Oliver will be hanging

00:02:29.700 --> 00:02:34.400
on to his English accent when he takes on
the role of Zazu, the same way Rowan Atkinson

00:02:34.400 --> 00:02:38.160
did when he lent his voice to the animated
character in 1994.

00:02:38.160 --> 00:02:42.290
The last movies where Oliver did some voice
acting were The Smurfs movies, which were

00:02:42.290 --> 00:02:45.680
pretty terrible, so he's got nowhere to go
but up!

00:02:45.680 --> 00:02:50.549
By the way, interestingly enough, Oliver previously
starred in the TV comedy Community alongside

00:02:50.549 --> 00:02:54.140
the new voice of Simba himself, Donald Glover.

00:02:54.140 --> 00:02:58.030
If you're wondering who'll be taking on the
role of Mufasa's wife and Simba's mother,

00:02:58.030 --> 00:03:02.600
Sarabi, it's Alfre Woodard, who's given fantastic
performances most recently as the corrupt

00:03:02.600 --> 00:03:07.459
councilwoman Mariah Dillard in Marvel's Luke
Cage and as the fearful Aunt Josephine in

00:03:07.459 --> 00:03:10.190
Netflix's A Series of Unfortunate Events.

00:03:10.190 --> 00:03:15.739
South African actor and playwright John Kani
is taking on the role of Rafiki, who teaches

00:03:15.739 --> 00:03:18.160
Simba some valuable lessons in the film.

00:03:18.160 --> 00:03:22.500
Like many of The Lion King cast, you'll have
seen Kani most recently in the MCU, where

00:03:22.500 --> 00:03:27.220
he played the Black Panther's father, King
T'Chaka, in Captain America: Civil War.

00:03:27.220 --> 00:03:32.129
Given how comedic the characters Pumbaa and
Timon are, Disney has wisely chosen to go

00:03:32.129 --> 00:03:34.500
with two comic actors for the new film.

00:03:34.500 --> 00:03:38.020
Star of Knocked-Up, Seth Rogen will be playing
warthog Pumbaa.

00:03:38.020 --> 00:03:41.849
But this certainly won't be Rogen's first
voice acting gig as he's already lent his

00:03:41.849 --> 00:03:46.900
vocal stylings to the Kung Fu Panda movies
as well as the more, er, adult animation,

00:03:46.900 --> 00:03:48.709
Sausage Party.

00:03:48.709 --> 00:03:52.459
Meanwhile Billy Eichner, who's best known
for his work on the comedy shows Difficult

00:03:52.459 --> 00:03:56.689
People, Parks And Rec, and Billy On The Street,
is taking on the role of the wise-cracking

00:03:56.689 --> 00:04:01.049
meerkat Timon, first brought to life by Nathan
Lane back in 1994.

00:04:01.049 --> 00:04:05.689
I've gotta say I'm kinda interested to see
what Seth Rogen and Billy Eichener's version

00:04:05.689 --> 00:04:07.469
of Hakuna Matata will be like.

00:04:07.469 --> 00:04:12.680
There are loads of Marvel connections among
the actors in this movie, and Florence Kasumba

00:04:12.680 --> 00:04:14.319
is no exception!

00:04:14.319 --> 00:04:18.620
In The Lion King, she'll be playing the hyena
Shenzi, who was originally voiced by Whoopi

00:04:18.620 --> 00:04:22.990
Goldberg, but if you've watched Captain America:
Civil War, then you'll have seen Kasumba face

00:04:22.990 --> 00:04:27.240
off with Black Widow as one of Black Panther's
elite female bodyguards, the Dora Milaje,

00:04:27.240 --> 00:04:33.440
and she'll be back in that role in the Black
Panther solo movie.

00:04:33.440 --> 00:04:38.000
Comic actors Keegan-Michael Key and Eric André,
best known for their respective TV series

00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:43.140
Key &amp; Peele and The Eric André Show, complete
the movie's trio of hyena characters.

00:04:43.140 --> 00:04:47.419
In the animated movie, the other two hyenas
were known as Banzai and Ed, but their names

00:04:47.419 --> 00:04:51.669
have been given a make-over for the new film,
with Key and André's characters being called

00:04:51.669 --> 00:04:54.320
Kamari and Azizi.

00:04:54.320 --> 00:04:58.990
Voicing the young Simba and Nala are relative
newcomers JD McCrary, who has a handful of

00:04:58.990 --> 00:05:03.780
TV credits to his name, and Shahadi Wright
Joseph, who appeared in the TV musical Hairspray

00:05:03.780 --> 00:05:04.780
Live!

00:05:04.780 --> 00:05:07.860
I'm sure Disney will have done as good a job
casting these important roles as they did

00:05:07.860 --> 00:05:09.940
with other recent films such as Moana.

00:05:09.940 --> 00:05:13.530
And I've got my fingers crossed that being
part of The Lion King cast brings great things

00:05:13.530 --> 00:05:15.380
for these two new young actors!

00:05:15.380 --> 00:05:19.841
Now, who's your favourite character from The
Lion King and how excited are you about the

00:05:19.841 --> 00:05:20.841
new cast?

00:05:20.841 --> 00:05:22.910
I'd love to hear your thoughts in the comments
below.

